 "descripcion": "Medieval brewsters paid small fines so often that the fines worked like a licence to brew. The end of a day with Agnes.\n\nWould you rather brew the ale, or taste it?\n\n#history #medieval #middleages #historyfacts #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "The ale passed. He was only frowning at the cold.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "But Agnes still pays a small fine, almost every month.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Fines were so common, they worked like a licence to brew.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "A real cheat, with weak ale or a short jug, got worse.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Some towns used a cucking stool, a chair to shame dishonest brewers.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "Tonight, the neighbours crowd around her fire, with full cups.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You fall asleep on the straw, smelling of malt.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "Would you rather brew the ale, or taste it?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
